{"id":"ekathotsarot","order":2624,"name":"Ekathotsarot","region":"southeast-asia","region_label":"Southeast Asia","realm":"King of Thailand","era":"early-modern","era_label":"Early Modern","blurb":null,"reign_from":1605,"reign_to":1610,"year_from":1605,"year_to":1610,"wp":"Ekathotsarot","source":"wikidata","civ_wiki":null,"sources":{"wikidata":"ok","wikipedia":"ok"},"qid":"Q882744","wikidata_url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q882744","wd_label":"Ekathotsarot","wd_description":"king of Ayutthaya","birth_year":1560,"death_year":1610,"reign_wikidata":[1590,1610],"image":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ekatotsarotwpamok06.jpg?width=640","family_qid":"Q16138308","predecessor_qid":null,"successor_qid":null,"father_qid":"Q888861","mother_qid":"Q6581540","children_qids":["Q13024810","Q889158","Q561528"],"birthplace_qid":"Q16305399","deathplace_qid":"Q542923","position_qids":["Q27330121","Q959495"],"family":"House of Sukhothai","predecessor":null,"successor":null,"predecessor_id":null,"successor_id":null,"father":"Maha Thammaracha","father_id":null,"mother":"Wisutkasat","children":["Suthat","Si Saowaphak","Songtham"],"birthplace":"Chan Royal Palace","birthplace_coord":[100.26133,16.82988],"deathplace":"Phra Ratchawang Boran","deathplace_coord":[100.55833,14.35861],"positions":["King of Thailand","Front Palace"],"extract":"Ekathotsarot (Thai: เอกาทศรถ, pronounced [ʔēː.kāː.tʰót.sā.rót], Ekādaśaratha) or Sanphet III (Thai: สรรเพชญ์ที่ ๓); 1560 – 1610/11) was the King of Ayutthaya from 1605 to 1610/11 and overlord of Lan Na from 1605 to 1608/09, succeeding his brother Naresuan. His reign was mostly peaceful as Siam was a powerful state through the conquests of Naresuan. It was also during his reign that foreigners of various origin began to fill the mercenary corps. In particular, the king had a regiment of professional Japanese guards under the command of Yamada Nagamasa.\nRight around Ekathotsarot's reign, the English first came to Siam in 1612.","wp_des